";
CM_ BO_ 2566840835 "Transmission Configuration : Total message length depends on total number of forward and reverse gear ratios.NOTE:  The first gear ratio transmitted in bytes 3,4 will be the highest reverse gear ratio.  Additional 2-byte gear ratios will follow:   3,4    Highest reverse gear ratio    .    .   a,b    Lowest reverse gear ratio   c,d    Lowest forward gear ratio    .    .   e,f    Highest forward gear ratio
VARIABLE_DLC_MESSAGE";
CM_ SG_ 2566840835 NumberofReverseGearRatios "SPN:958 VVR:[0,250]
Number of reverse gear ratios in the transmission, provided as part of the transmission configuration.";
CM_ SG_ 2566840835 NumberofForwardGearRatios "SPN:957 VVR:[0,250]
Number of forward gear ratios in the transmission, provided as part of the configuration.";
CM_ SG_ 2566840835 TransmissionGearRatio "SPN:581 VVR:[0,64255]
The transmission configuration describes the number of forward gears, the number of reverse gears, and the ratio of each gear with the following resolution.";
CM_ BO_ 2364539395 "Electronic Transmission Controller 1 : Electronic Transmission Controller #1Note:Single input shaft transmissions should use SPN 161 (Transmission Input Shaft Speed)";
CM_ SG_ 2364539395 TransmissionDrivelineEngaged "SPN:560
Driveline engaged indicates the transmission controlled portion of the driveline is engaged sufficiently to allow a transfer of torque through the transmission.  ";
CM_ SG_ 2364539395 TransTrqConverterLockupEngaged "SPN:573 VVR:[0,1]
State signal which indicates whether the torque converter lockup is engaged.
00 Torque converter lockup disengaged
01 Torque converter lockup engaged
10 Error
11 Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2364539395 TransmissionShiftInProcess "SPN:574
Indicates that the transmission is in process of shifting from the current gear to the selected gear. This state is generally ACTIVE during the entire time that the transmission controls the vehicle during a shift. This includes any transmission clutch control, all engine control sequences, pulling to transmission neutral, and engaging the destination gear (e.g., until it is no longer sending commands and/or limits to the engine). See also SPN 560. (See Figure SPN574_A)";
CM_ SG_ 2364539395 TransmissionOutputShaftSpeed "SPN:191 VVR:[0,64255]
Calculated speed of the transmission output shaft.";
CM_ SG_ 2364539395 PercentClutchSlip "SPN:522 VVR:[0,250]
Parameter which represents the ratio of input shaft speed to current engine speed (in percent).
Percent Clutch Slip = ((Engine rpm - Input shaft rpm)/(Engine rpm)) x 100";
CM_ SG_ 2364539395 ProgressiveShiftDisable "SPN:607 VVR:[0,1]
Command signal used to indicate that progressive shifting by the engine should be disallowed.
00 Progressive shift is not disabled
01 Progressive shift is disabled
10 Reserved
11 Take no action";
CM_ SG_ 2364539395 TransmissionInputShaftSpeed "SPN:161 VVR:[0,64255]
Rotational velocity of the primary shaft transferring power into the transmission.  When a torque converter is present, it is the output of the torque converter.";
CM_ BO_ 2566801923 "Electronic Transmission Controller 7 : Transmission status information from the transmission controller to network.";
CM_ SG_ 2566801923 TransmissionReadyforBrakeRelease "SPN:3086
This parameter indicates that enough torque / motive force is available at the transmission output shaft to release all the brakes without a risk of unintentional movement in the opposite direction.";
CM_ SG_ 2566801923 TransmissionEngineCrankEnable "SPN:2900 VVR:[0,1]
State signal from the transmission indicating if the transmissions status is such that engine cranking is allowed (i.e.  at a minimum, transmission is in neutral and the driveline is disengaged). ";
CM_ SG_ 2566801923 TransmissionMode2Indicator "SPN:2537
This state signal is the transmissions indication that it is operating under transmission mode 2 (SPN 1853) as commanded via the TC1 message (PGN 256). ";
CM_ SG_ 2566801923 TransmissionMode1Indicator "SPN:2536
This state signal is the transmissions indication that it is operating under transmission mode 1 (SPN 1852) as commanded via the TC1 message (PGN 256).  The definition of the transmission mode is left to the discretion of the transmission manufacturer.
00 Transmission Mode 1 not active
01 Transmission Mode 1 Active
10 Error
11 Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2566801923 TransmissionMode6Indicator "SPN:4251
This state signal is the transmissions indication that it is operating under transmission mode 6 (SPN 4247) as commanded via the TC1 message (PGN 256).";
CM_ SG_ 2566801923 TransmissionMode7Indicator "SPN:4252
This state signal is the transmissions indication that it is operating under transmission mode 7 (SPN 4248) as commanded via the TC1 message (PGN 256).";
CM_ SG_ 2566801923 TransmissionMode8Indicator "SPN:4253
This state signal is the transmissions indication that it is operating under transmission mode 8 (SPN 4249) as commanded via the TC1 message (PGN 256). ";
